    "biography": {
      "concept": "The forest's champion on the Fixit road; speaks only in road signs (Act 2)",
      "notes": "The Tree Person of Early Tifaret is the forest's champion: a big, aggressive tree person with old highway tangled in its roots, asphalt, a mile-marker and somewhere in there a bus stop. It speaks only in road signs, one at a time, in capitals (YIELD, MERGE, NO OUTLET, ROAD WORK AHEAD) and it means every one of them. It is not being funny; it is being clear. It holds up signs the way other people hold up hands, and when it is pleased it turns one over."
    }
